Source landscape: Discovery produced a broad, multilingual source universe spanning ruler biographies and profiles, Sharif-family and Pakistani political histories, official government records, international-organization assessments, NGO reports, economic and security studies, election analyses, scholarly work, and later retrospectives. The strongest clusters concern fiscal crisis and IMF negotiations, democratic transition and civil liberties, military–civilian relations, governance capacity, Punjab administrative legacy, terrorism and domestic security, flood recovery, and Pakistan’s external relations. Several catalogue-only, preview-only, paywalled, and potentially partisan works are retained for later evidence screening. Searches included English and Urdu variants, including “Shehbaz,” “Shahbaz,” and “Shahbaz Sharif.”

